WEBVTT

00:00:01.147 --> 00:00:06.017
Yume kara samete mo
Even if I wake from my dreams

00:00:07.057 --> 00:00:12.517
Kono te wo nobasu yo
I'll reach my hand out to you

00:00:24.037 --> 00:00:29.307
Onaji tsuyosa de yobi au
If our hearts can reach each other

00:00:30.047 --> 00:00:34.747
Kokoro ni nareru no naraba
with the same strength

00:00:35.987 --> 00:00:41.247
Nanninbun no kizu demo
Then I would be able to bare

00:00:41.787 --> 00:00:46.917
Boku wa uketome rareru yo
The pain of many hearts

00:00:47.327 --> 00:00:50.857
Mousukoshi datte kiga surun da
I can feel that it will arrive soon

00:00:50.927 --> 00:00:55.797
Kono kabe ga kuzureru
When these walls will be torn down

00:00:56.607 --> 00:01:01.007
Reimei
The dawn

00:01:02.747 --> 00:01:08.707
Yume kara samete mo
mada minai yume no houmade
Even if we wake from our dreams
We'll have to keep running

00:01:08.787 --> 00:01:14.687
Bokura wa hitori de
hashiri tuzukeru shika nain da
Towards our unrevealed dreams

00:01:14.757 --> 00:01:21.317
Korogari mayotte tsukuri dasu
boku no inryoku ga
The gravity by my painful journey
will draw me

00:01:21.597 --> 00:01:27.537
Itsuka kimi e
To you one day

00:01:54.197 --> 00:01:55.387
What was that?

00:01:55.697 --> 00:01:58.397
Weren't we just here?

00:02:05.977 --> 00:02:07.527
We were transported?

00:02:21.587 --> 00:02:23.177
A transporting device?

00:02:23.727 --> 00:02:26.317
Maybe we should go
back to those pillars.

00:02:27.097 --> 00:02:28.827
Let's go somewhere else.

00:02:28.997 --> 00:02:33.027
Maybe we'll find the same thing
in the other Lost Grounds.

00:02:33.137 --> 00:02:35.467
Remember, we're looking
for the Virus Cores!

00:02:35.907 --> 00:02:40.037
I doubt those patterns have anything
to do with the Virus Cores.

00:02:40.807 --> 00:02:41.967
We don't know that.

00:02:42.147 --> 00:02:43.907
They could have something
to do with each other.

00:02:44.147 --> 00:02:45.377
Come on, let's go!

00:02:47.447 --> 00:02:48.847
Fine.

00:02:49.147 --> 00:02:50.947
Haseo, we're going
to the next place.

00:02:51.317 --> 00:02:51.837
Oh, yeah.

00:03:01.027 --> 00:03:02.397
Amazing!

00:03:02.597 --> 00:03:04.067
What is this place?

00:03:04.867 --> 00:03:05.957
It's your first time here?

00:03:06.037 --> 00:03:06.627
Yeah.

00:03:06.767 --> 00:03:08.467
You've been here before?

00:03:15.907 --> 00:03:20.037
There used to be a statue of
a girl here a long time ago.

00:03:20.517 --> 00:03:21.707
That's right, Haseo.

00:03:22.147 --> 00:03:25.177
This game has a very
mysterious autonomy.

00:03:26.017 --> 00:03:26.717
Aura.

00:03:27.517 --> 00:03:29.247
That was her name.

00:03:29.727 --> 00:03:33.557
Neither the system administrator
nor any outsider can control it.

00:03:33.827 --> 00:03:37.887
Parts of it are controlled by
the rules of the game itself.

00:03:38.767 --> 00:03:41.397
Well, maybe she just lost
interest in the end...

00:03:42.167 --> 00:03:43.797
...and lost hope for this world.

00:03:44.267 --> 00:03:45.637
It exists.

00:03:45.907 --> 00:03:48.837
You must play this game with
the assumption that it exists.

00:03:50.147 --> 00:03:52.877
That's why we are
the Twilight Brigade.

00:04:02.457 --> 00:04:03.887
Are you in the bathroom, Haseo?

00:04:05.327 --> 00:04:06.887
Hurry up, guys!

00:04:06.957 --> 00:04:08.117
Okay!

00:04:09.797 --> 00:04:10.727
Let's go!

00:04:11.467 --> 00:04:12.057
Hey!

00:04:29.917 --> 00:04:32.287
How are we supposed
to find them?

00:04:34.357 --> 00:04:38.917
I don't think it'll be easy finding
this item that's not in the specs.

00:04:47.737 --> 00:04:49.827
I've never seen you like that.

00:04:50.467 --> 00:04:51.797
Never mind.

00:04:51.877 --> 00:04:53.267
I mean, I don't think
there's anything here.

00:04:53.607 --> 00:04:56.877
They wouldn't leave some obvious
treasure box in a place like this.

00:04:58.447 --> 00:05:00.207
This isn't a normal area...

00:05:00.277 --> 00:05:02.877
...so I thought maybe the
Virus Cores could be here.

00:05:04.417 --> 00:05:06.117
Didn't Shino tell you?

00:05:06.787 --> 00:05:09.277
The Lost Grounds
are abnormal areas...

00:05:09.357 --> 00:05:11.047
...that nobody can touch.

00:05:11.227 --> 00:05:12.517
I've heard that already.

00:05:12.657 --> 00:05:16.057
Not even the administrator
can close or delete it.

00:05:16.697 --> 00:05:19.327
An area that appears and
disappears randomly.

00:05:19.737 --> 00:05:21.287
Just like that last transport.

00:05:21.567 --> 00:05:24.127
That would have been impossible
in the normal areas.

00:05:24.507 --> 00:05:25.567
I guess.

00:05:25.907 --> 00:05:29.167
In the Lost Grounds,
it becomes possible.

00:05:32.047 --> 00:05:32.567
Tabby?!

00:05:34.147 --> 00:05:34.947
Where is she?

00:05:35.087 --> 00:05:36.517
Tabby, where are you?

00:05:36.687 --> 00:05:38.807
Haseo, send Tabby an email.

00:05:38.917 --> 00:05:39.217
Huh?

00:05:39.517 --> 00:05:40.147
Quickly!

00:05:41.457 --> 00:05:43.647
She was looking in this area.

00:05:47.427 --> 00:05:49.487
I don't think the email went through.

00:05:52.897 --> 00:05:55.227
Sakisaka, where are you?!

00:06:03.477 --> 00:06:04.237
Oh?

00:06:04.877 --> 00:06:06.007
Are you alone?

00:06:07.377 --> 00:06:09.217
Aren't your friends with you?

00:06:11.217 --> 00:06:13.487
That's none of your business.

00:06:14.257 --> 00:06:15.487
Oh, how cold.

00:06:15.887 --> 00:06:17.517
Don't hide things from me.

00:06:19.327 --> 00:06:20.487
Where did they go?

00:06:21.057 --> 00:06:24.027
Three came in here, but
there's only one now.

00:06:24.367 --> 00:06:25.267
What's going on?

00:06:27.497 --> 00:06:30.127
If you don't answer me,
you might die.

00:06:34.007 --> 00:06:35.497
Something's come up.

00:06:35.807 --> 00:06:36.837
See you later.

00:06:55.397 --> 00:06:57.297
Who has the Virus Core?

00:06:57.427 --> 00:06:59.157
If you don't tell me, I'll PK you!

00:06:59.237 --> 00:07:02.257
Are you purposely fighting us
just because we're from Kestrel?

00:07:02.507 --> 00:07:03.127
Yeah.

00:07:03.467 --> 00:07:04.907
You have a problem with that?

00:07:05.807 --> 00:07:08.207
It's only a rumor.
I don't know anything about it.

00:07:08.577 --> 00:07:10.767
I swear!
I don't know anything!

00:07:11.107 --> 00:07:12.077
You're useless.

00:07:12.147 --> 00:07:15.377
Fine. Revive him
and get out of here.

00:07:16.887 --> 00:07:17.977
Rip Maen.

00:07:22.957 --> 00:07:25.547
Sorry, sorry!
I got stuck at work.

00:07:26.357 --> 00:07:28.227
So, what was that all about?

00:07:28.467 --> 00:07:31.027
My way of collecting information.

00:07:31.937 --> 00:07:34.337
Using violence to get it
out of them, huh?

00:07:34.797 --> 00:07:36.667
More importantly,
did you find something?

00:07:36.837 --> 00:07:38.097
I did, but...

00:07:38.237 --> 00:07:38.727
What?

00:07:39.137 --> 00:07:40.437
It's going to be trouble.

00:07:40.677 --> 00:07:43.577
Rumor has it that
it's someone from Kestrel.

00:07:43.647 --> 00:07:44.577
Who is it?

00:07:45.007 --> 00:07:47.107
You know Bordeaux?

00:07:47.477 --> 00:07:48.347
The player killer?

00:07:48.817 --> 00:07:51.307
It fell into her hands
purely by chance.

00:07:52.617 --> 00:07:53.547
Interesting.

00:07:59.557 --> 00:08:00.487
Welcome back.

00:08:01.357 --> 00:08:02.757
They're not back yet?

00:08:03.297 --> 00:08:04.527
I heard about what happened.

00:08:05.937 --> 00:08:08.997
Sakisaka is working
independently now.

00:08:09.807 --> 00:08:11.537
But Sakisaka disappeared!

00:08:11.937 --> 00:08:12.457
Yes.

00:08:12.807 --> 00:08:14.327
I'll explain.

00:08:14.907 --> 00:08:17.467
I think Tabby will
be back soon as well.

00:08:28.927 --> 00:08:30.047
He's out?

00:08:35.097 --> 00:08:35.717
What are you doing?

00:08:36.627 --> 00:08:37.787
Ender!

00:08:37.927 --> 00:08:40.057
I wanted to ask you something.

00:08:40.137 --> 00:08:41.537
What is it?

00:08:41.597 --> 00:08:43.867
Apparently, there're more of these.

00:08:44.707 --> 00:08:47.797
Don't you think
it's a bad idea to keep that here?

00:08:48.207 --> 00:08:50.677
But I can't just let it go.

00:08:51.077 --> 00:08:53.167
Either way, someone will come for it.

00:08:53.747 --> 00:08:55.717
So, what about you?

00:08:55.917 --> 00:08:58.317
Haven't they made a move yet?

00:08:58.617 --> 00:08:59.587
They disappeared.

00:09:01.257 --> 00:09:04.017
Anyway, they'll probably
meet up at Mac Anu...

00:09:04.087 --> 00:09:05.687
...so I'm resting until then.

00:09:05.757 --> 00:09:07.197
What do you mean "disappeared"?

00:09:08.027 --> 00:09:11.727
Do you know anything about
the scars in the Lost Grounds?

00:09:12.137 --> 00:09:12.857
Oh!

00:09:13.337 --> 00:09:15.997
The scars that distort the graphics.

00:09:16.307 --> 00:09:19.137
I was thinking I should
name them pretty soon.

00:09:19.577 --> 00:09:22.237
After all, TaN is on the
leading edge of any trend.

00:09:22.647 --> 00:09:23.607
So, what about it?

00:09:24.277 --> 00:09:26.577
There's a transporting
function to them.

00:09:27.247 --> 00:09:29.837
So that's how you lost them.

00:09:30.447 --> 00:09:31.147
Where?

00:09:31.617 --> 00:09:33.107
I didn't lose them.

00:09:33.457 --> 00:09:34.647
It doesn't matter.

00:09:34.717 --> 00:09:35.447
So where was it?

00:09:36.157 --> 00:09:37.387
The Hulle Granz Cathedral.

00:09:37.757 --> 00:09:38.727
Oh!

00:09:38.797 --> 00:09:41.417
The Lost Ground that
was just discovered.

00:09:45.567 --> 00:09:48.587
So there's someone
named Bordeaux there?

00:09:49.467 --> 00:09:51.337
Can I ask you something?

00:09:51.407 --> 00:09:53.637
If it's a question I can answer.

00:09:53.707 --> 00:09:57.537
Why are you trying so hard
to get the Virus Cores...

00:09:57.607 --> 00:09:59.637
...and why "defeat Ovan"?

00:10:00.517 --> 00:10:03.417
To make him see that I'm better.

00:10:09.187 --> 00:10:10.777
How childish!

00:10:18.997 --> 00:10:21.527
...and before I knew it
I was inside the wall...

00:10:21.597 --> 00:10:23.827
...and there were these weird lines.

00:10:23.907 --> 00:10:27.037
And I tried real hard to move...

00:10:27.107 --> 00:10:30.237
...but I couldn't, so I
had to force terminate.

00:10:30.447 --> 00:10:31.997
So what happened to Sakisaka?

00:10:33.377 --> 00:10:35.817
He's working alone now.

00:10:36.847 --> 00:10:40.307
Sakisaka got hit by a bug
like you did.

00:10:40.517 --> 00:10:43.547
But he came back right away,
so I gave him an assignment.

00:10:43.627 --> 00:10:45.117
That's my teacher!

00:10:46.027 --> 00:10:48.857
I, on the other hand,
was struggling for a while.

00:10:49.197 --> 00:10:52.427
And I didn't even realize
it was a bug right away.

00:10:52.797 --> 00:10:55.597
And after hearing about
what happened to Haseo...

00:10:55.667 --> 00:10:58.867
...I think it's too dangerous for
the three of you to work together.

00:10:58.937 --> 00:10:59.907
What do you mean?

00:11:00.537 --> 00:11:03.837
Ender showed up after you
and Sakisaka disappeared.

00:11:04.247 --> 00:11:04.867
What?!

00:11:05.377 --> 00:11:10.007
It's likely you're being followed.
You can never be too cautious.

00:11:12.217 --> 00:11:14.517
So, what are we
supposed to do now?

00:11:14.757 --> 00:11:18.887
Tabby, I want you to continue
searching for the Virus Cores.

00:11:19.957 --> 00:11:20.547
Okay!

00:11:21.427 --> 00:11:22.057
What about me?

00:11:22.767 --> 00:11:26.497
I'd like you to check out
the information you brought.

00:11:26.937 --> 00:11:27.927
Information?

00:11:28.367 --> 00:11:30.027
Um...

00:11:30.107 --> 00:11:32.867
The information about
how to get to where...

00:11:33.237 --> 00:11:34.327
...the Key of the Twilight is...

00:11:34.507 --> 00:11:37.967
...and how you have to use
items that aren't in the specs.

00:11:38.407 --> 00:11:39.677
You brought it, right?

00:11:39.917 --> 00:11:40.437
Yeah.

00:11:42.147 --> 00:11:43.177
I'll leave it to you.

00:11:56.167 --> 00:11:59.457
This'll be painless if
you just hand it over.

00:11:59.897 --> 00:12:02.227
Is this really that important?

00:12:02.507 --> 00:12:04.767
It's useless to you.

00:12:05.107 --> 00:12:06.227
Right...

00:12:06.437 --> 00:12:08.497
I guess it's okay...

00:12:08.977 --> 00:12:11.167
...to be a PKK every
once in a while!

00:12:16.617 --> 00:12:17.877
You're still here?

00:12:22.127 --> 00:12:25.817
The items that aren't in the specs
are these Virus Cores, right?

00:12:26.427 --> 00:12:27.227
Probably.

00:12:34.597 --> 00:12:35.367
Look!

00:12:36.107 --> 00:12:37.897
How many are there?

00:12:38.337 --> 00:12:42.277
The rumors say there's as many of
these as there are Lost Grounds.

00:12:42.607 --> 00:12:43.597
So, six?

00:12:43.777 --> 00:12:46.537
But isn't it interesting that
they're different colors?

00:12:46.717 --> 00:12:48.407
Maybe they're all different colors.

00:13:01.857 --> 00:13:04.087
You can't win against me!

00:13:06.137 --> 00:13:09.257
Kudos to you for having the
courage to fight by yourself.

00:13:09.737 --> 00:13:12.137
But it's pointless if you can't win.

00:13:17.807 --> 00:13:20.607
They say carelessness
is your worst enemy.

00:13:21.217 --> 00:13:22.947
I'm a pro at fooling people.

00:13:22.947 --> 00:13:23.847
W-Wait!

00:13:24.587 --> 00:13:25.647
You can have it!

00:13:25.717 --> 00:13:26.887
So, give us a break?

00:13:26.887 --> 00:13:29.077
That was easy.

00:13:29.157 --> 00:13:31.287
Always know your limits.

00:13:38.167 --> 00:13:39.457
That bastard!

00:13:42.067 --> 00:13:44.267
You going to behave
yourself and give it to me?

00:13:45.267 --> 00:13:46.537
Who are you?

00:13:47.037 --> 00:13:49.527
Saving the weak!
Defeating the strong!

00:13:49.607 --> 00:13:52.667
You can call me
the PK of Justice!

00:13:54.177 --> 00:13:55.377
Fine, then!

00:13:56.487 --> 00:13:57.247
Here you go!

00:14:03.687 --> 00:14:04.957
I'll take this.

00:14:08.827 --> 00:14:12.957
Trust is the most important
thing to a merchant.

00:14:13.467 --> 00:14:16.127
I wonder how
I should hand it over.

00:14:37.687 --> 00:14:38.347
What's the matter?

00:14:38.427 --> 00:14:39.117
Just come!

00:14:45.897 --> 00:14:48.197
The color of the light
on that pillar is different...

00:14:48.267 --> 00:14:49.967
...than the light in
that pillar, right?

00:14:50.037 --> 00:14:51.467
It seems like it.

00:14:52.637 --> 00:14:55.167
I think the Virus Cores are
supposed to be used here.

00:14:58.207 --> 00:14:58.937
Haseo!

00:14:59.477 --> 00:15:00.537
Only three more.

00:15:01.017 --> 00:15:04.777
We need to find the colors that
match the rest of these pillars.

00:15:05.317 --> 00:15:08.647
Five Virus Cores plus
one for the final stage.

00:15:08.957 --> 00:15:12.087
That means there are as
many as the Lost Grounds!

00:15:12.327 --> 00:15:13.557
We have to tell Ovan!

00:15:13.757 --> 00:15:14.727
I'll tell him.

00:15:24.607 --> 00:15:28.037
What will you do if you find
the Key of the Twilight?

00:15:28.307 --> 00:15:29.177
I don't know.

00:15:29.677 --> 00:15:30.507
What about you?

00:15:31.147 --> 00:15:32.137
I'll...

00:15:33.447 --> 00:15:34.637
I think I'll keep it a secret.

00:15:35.347 --> 00:15:36.477
